---
Analyze local PyTorch profiler traces and render an HTML report

Usage: comms_viz [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --trace-root <TRACE_ROOT>      Directory holding one step's profiler traces, one file per rank (e.g. TorchTitan's `profile_traces/iteration_<N>/`)
  -o, --out <OUT>                    Output root for analysis artifacts
      --report <DIR>                 Directory in which to write the HTML report and its data sidecars [default: <out>/report]
      --structured-report <DIR>      Directory in which to write a structured report: the HTML report's data and derived tables as Markdown and CSV [default: <out>/structured_report]
      --run-id <RUN_ID>              Run identifier used in the artifact tree. Defaults to `local-run`, or `local-run-<N>` if that run already exists under `--out`
      --overwrite                    Replace an existing run with the same id under `--out`
      --run-name <RUN_NAME>          Descriptive run name shown in the report
      --trace-format <TRACE_FORMAT>  Trace format: auto, json, or pftrace [default: auto]
      --write-repaired-traces        Also write each rank's trace after the CUDA-graph repair to `tree/<run>/traces/`, for viewing in Perfetto
  -v, --verbose                      Print per-rank analysis time
  -h, --help                         Print help

Analyze and render: `comms_viz --trace-root ./traces --out ./analysis --report ./report`
Render existing artifacts: `comms_viz --out ./analysis --report ./report`
